Just wanted to say thank-you to @joshtriplett & @m-ou-se (and everyone else who has input into design and implementation since I originally drafted the RFC). 

I'm really excited to see this landing - I stumbled on this idea when I was trying to find words to explain Rust's string formatting macros to beginners, and I think this syntax will be a nice way to simplify how we can introduce users to their first `println!` invocation.

```
fn main() {
    let target = "World";
    println!("Hello, {target}");
}
```

... just seems a little easier to beginners to have intuition about than `println!("Hello, {}", target)`.

 On top of that, I'm definitely planning to use this a lot in my own code 😂

